Why do you think that changing the medium to a similar (but usually
technically inferior[1]) one would change the idea finding *and*
implementation process?

Talk on a web forum is first and foremost nothing else than just talk.

If nobody implements it it stays the same as most YANIs in this group:
talk.

But this group has a big advantage with Google Groups searchable index
that won't go away. If I have an idea to do something I look first in
here if somebody else had a better idea about that concept. So to me,
this group and its history had a large influence on NetHack.

There is also a realtime chat community for NetHack: IRC.

But I've never seen a good idea on IRC that hasn't been discussed in
here more thoroughly.

Brainstorming isn't all about getting ideas in real time you also need
to choose the good one and elaborate on them. And that is nothing you
can do well in a realtime medium. It's hard to get a good discussion
on IRC between more than two or three people.

Bye
Patric

[1] Most forum software that is in use and that I know is pretty
